{"id":"ru_ckzug","lemma":"Rückzug","pos":"noun","rank":3298,"glosses":["retreat"],"ipa":"/ˈʁykˌtsuːk/","audio":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/7/7d/De-R%C3%BCckzug.ogg/De-R%C3%BCckzug.ogg.mp3","gender":"m","forms":{"genitive":"Rückzuges","plural":"Rückzüge"},"examples":[{"text":"Der General gab Befehl zum Rückzug.","en":"The general gave the order to retreat.","words":[{"g":"the"},{"g":"general"},{"g":"to give","l":"geben"},{"g":"command, order"},{"g":"to the"},null]},{"text":"Sie wurden zum Rückzug gezwungen.","en":"They were forced to withdraw.","words":[{"g":"she / they / you"},{"g":"to become","l":"werden"},{"g":"to the"},null,{"g":"to force","l":"zwingen"}]},{"text":"Ihnen blieb nur der Rückzug.","en":"They had no alternative but to retreat.","words":[{"g":"(to) them","l":"sie"},{"g":"to remain","l":"bleiben"},{"g":"only"},{"g":"the"},null]},{"text":"Die sowjetischen Truppen haben mit dem Rückzug aus Afghanistan begonnen.","en":"The Soviet troops started to withdraw from Afghanistan.","words":[{"g":"the"},{"g":"Soviet","l":"sowjetisch"},{"g":"troupe","l":"Truppe"},{"g":"have"},{"g":"with"},{"g":"(to) the","l":"der"},null,{"g":"out of / from"},null,{"g":"to begin","l":"beginnen"}]}]}